    "q-166839": {
      "dom_id": "question-166839",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Which slice ($A,$ $B,$ or $C$) of the cake slices from part 1 corresponds to a right angle?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Slice$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "In part 1, we found that $z={7}^{∘}.$ \n\nWe substitute it into the expression for angles and obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =23({7}^{∘})+{4}^{∘}={165}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & =12({7}^{∘})+{6}^{∘}={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠C & =15({7}^{∘})={105}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, slice $B$ corresponds to a right angle.",
