    "q-166841": {
      "dom_id": "question-166841",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "How many cakes does the pastry shop produce if they use equal numbers of packs of flour and butter?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The pastry shop produces$\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$cakes.",
      "worked_solution": "To produce $x$ cakes, the pastry shop uses the following amounts:\n\n- $\\frac{4x+1}{6}$ packs of butter\n\n- $\\frac{13x+5}{20}$ packs of flour\n\nIf the pastry shop uses the same number of packs of butter and flour, we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x+1}{6}=\\frac{13x+5}{20}.\n$$\n\nWe need to solve this linear equation for $x.$ First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x+1}{6} & =\\frac{13x+5}{20} \\\\ (4x+1)\\cdot 20 & =6\\cdot (13x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4x+1)\\cdot 20 & =6\\cdot (13x+5) \\\\ 80x+20 & =78x+30 \\\\ 80x+20-78x & =78x+30-78x \\\\ 2x+20 & =30 \\\\ 2x+20-20 & =30-20 \\\\ 2x & =10 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $x=5$ cakes are produced when the pastry shop uses the same number of packs of butter and flour.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
